window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"heimerdinger","b":"locke","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Locke","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Level 3 nest","text":"Three turrets up — his gap-close engage becomes suicide into the nest."},{"when":"Enemy 6 + first item","text":"Purgatory executes an immobile Heimer off his nest — never walk the lane naked."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Super-turrets plus the E stun zone him out — the standoff resumes on your terms."},{"text":"Late fights come down to one number: Ashen Pursuit is a flat 10s and it is his engage and his only exit. Every time he spends it your team has ten seconds against a Locke who cannot leave the turret beams.","when":"Late fights"}],"wants":{"you":["A full nest before every trade","Turret cover whenever HP dips","Stun-punishes on his all-in dives"],"foe":["A catch between your nests","First-item execute picks","Baited turrets, then the jump"]},"early":"The lane is a fortress war that stays even as long as the fortress stands: your turret nest holds his melee threat at arm's length, W rockets match his chip, and his gap-close into three turrets is just a donation. Keep the nest full, save the E stun for the moment he jumps, and only ever take fights from inside your own setup.","mid":"From his 6 through first item, an immobile Heimerdinger caught off his nest is an executed Heimerdinger — Purgatory converts any catch. Walk the lane only with turrets in pocket, ward the flanks he would jump from, and keep your HP out of threshold range. Inside the nest you are still untouchable; this entire window is about never being outside it.","late":"Two-plus items restores the standoff with better toys: UPGRADE!!! super-turrets and your E stun zone entire chunks of the map, and one landed grenade on his engage deletes him inside the nest. Siege with your team around your setup, re-nest before every fight, and make him choose between diving into stun-plus-turrets or watching his towers fall.","whys":["Level 1 is even — your turret range holds his melee threat out, but he can punish any overextension past it.","Level 2 stays skill — W rockets match his passive chip evenly.","Level 3 is even: the turret nest blanks his E gap-close — he jumps in and the nest chews him.","Levels 4-5 stay a skill war over turret clears and dodging your grenade.","Level 6 keeps it even — Purgatory is 120s and the fortress standoff holds while his items are missing.","First item is Locke's — Purgatory plus a Lich Bane blink-bite executes an immobile Heimerdinger caught off the nest; play tight.","2+ items returns to skill — UPGRADE!!! super-turrets and the E stun zone his approach, and one landed stun deletes him."]});
